=== zh_0570 ===
// source: "A Diary Page, Author Unknown"
一页无名日记
-> DONE

=== zh_0571 ===
// source: "If the truth of death itself is being covered up, then am I not an accomplice when I carve monuments to that lie?\n\nI can no longer bear this hypocritical world. If even one person had stopped to question what was wrong with the world we lived in, perhaps we would never have come to this.\n\nI once loved and respected my mother so much. She was my example from childhood. But first she failed to protect my brother; then she blamed my father's disappearance on others. Even when I tried to tell her the truth about our world, she insisted that useless sympathy would destroy Day City.\n\nHow many more times must we hurt our own people in the name of protecting them?\n\nShe left me a message on my windowsill when she came to the Day City. She is so intelligent that she acquired the language of Day City just by observing the surroundings and reading the library, and she found out my identity as her correspondence just by the messages conveyed by the stones. She said there was an old site in the ruins, with sleeping coffins that could keep the two of us alive.\n\nShe told me why she wanted to leave. Before her brother was born, she had a place in the family. Afterwards, every hope and every tenderness seemed to belong to him. When he disappeared, she waited for her parents to notice that she was still there. Instead, their grief filled the place he had left. Night City called them the Holy Father and Holy Mother. She could not remember the last time she had felt like their daughter.\n\nI wanted to leave a world my mother kept defending. She wanted to leave a home where she felt unseen. Neither of us would bring our mother. With my mother's influence in Day City, everyone would find out if she came. For the other girl, leaving without hers was the point.\n\nI have to persuade her. We can only escape on our own. The One-way Passage Order is launching soon. We need to act fast."
如果连死亡的真相都被遮掩，我为谎言刻碑，难道就不是共犯吗？

我再也受不了这个虚伪的世界。哪怕曾有一个人停下来问问，我们活着的这个世界到底哪里出了问题，也许事情就不会走到这一步。

我曾那么爱、那么敬重母亲。小时候她就是我的榜样。可她没能保护弟弟，又把父亲的消失怪到别人头上。就连我试着告诉她这个世界的真相时，她也坚持说，无用的同情会毁了昼城。

我们还要打着保护自己人的旗号，伤害自己人多少次？

她来昼城时，在我的窗台上留了消息。她很聪明，光靠观察和读图书馆里的书就学会了昼城的语言，又靠碑上传递的消息认出了我是她的另一半。她说废墟里有一处旧址，那里的睡棺能让我们两个活下去。

她告诉我她为什么想走。弟弟出生以前，家里有她的位置。后来，所有期待和温柔都好像只给了弟弟。弟弟消失后，她等着父母注意到自己还在。可是他们的悲痛填满了弟弟留下的空位。夜城叫他们圣父和圣母。她已经记不起上一次觉得自己是他们的女儿是什么时候了。

我想离开母亲一直维护的世界。她想离开那个没人看见她的家。我们谁也不会带上母亲。以我母亲在昼城的影响力，她要是同行，所有人都会知道。而对那个女孩来说，能不带上母亲，才是离开的意义。

我得说服她。我们只能自己逃走。《单向通行令》很快就要实施。得快一点。
-> DONE

