// source: "Moon-shaped offerings"
月形祭品
-> DONE

=== zh_0601 ===
// source: "Yes, it does look like a moon. I suppose sleep is the closest rehearsal the living have for death. When night falls, the Dayfolk slip into slumber. On this marker, the moon stands for natural death."
是的，确实像月亮。对活着的人来说，睡眠大概最接近对死亡的预演。夜幕一落，昼民便沉入睡眠。在这座碑上，月亮代表自然死亡。
-> DONE

=== zh_0602 ===
// source: "The moon offers a peaceful ending, but that is the story the family chose to put in stone. If the child's real face was left out, perhaps there were unexplained circumstances behind his death. Let us keep looking."
月亮给了他一个平静的结尾，那也是家人选来刻在石头上的说法。如果孩子真实的脸被省去了，他的死或许也另有隐情。继续查吧。
-> DONE

=== zh_0603 ===
// source: "Before we ask why, perhaps we should ask why not. Day City remembers a life through its work. This child was the first to die without an identifiable occupation. So the designer gave him something no title was needed for: the shape of a person."
在问为什么之前，或许可以先问一句，为什么不呢？昼城以职业纪念一个人的一生。这位婴儿是第一个离世时还没有职业的人。设计师便给了他一种无需头衔的形状：一个人的形状。
-> DONE

=== zh_0604 ===
// source: "As the manuscript says, they gave her the title Scholar when she discovered what the crystal could do. Her stone remembers that work in the very material she studied—the work she was truly proud of."
就像手稿写的那样。她发现晶石的用途之后，得到了学者的称号。她的碑用她研究过的材料记下了这份工作，也是她真正引以为傲的事。
-> DONE

=== zh_0605 ===
// source: "The old account says the creature vanished in a single night. These little figures seem to carry that absence from stone to stone. They record disappearance. You may find other traces of what disappearance meant for the Dayfolk."
传说里，那只兽一夜之间消失了。那些小兽好像把这份缺席从一座碑带到了下一座。它们记的是消失。你或许还能找到别的痕迹，看看消失对昼民意味着什么。
-> DONE

=== zh_0606 ===
// source: "So many stones have borrowed the same creature. Its vanishing in the old account gives the carving its meaning: disappearance. An image left behind where a life cannot be found."
这么多座碑都借用了同一只兽。旧记载里它消失了，所以刻像代表消失。找不到那条生命，留下的只有它的形象。
-> DONE

=== zh_0607 ===
// source: "Day City records a death. Night City records a disappearance. That difference does not mean there were two children. Check the figures together."
昼城记录了一场死亡，夜城记录了一次消失。记法不同，不一定是两个孩子。把两个人形放在一起看看。
-> DONE

=== zh_0608 ===
// source: "That is the altar infant. The figure is his mother in Night City."
那是祭坛上的婴儿。抱他的是他在夜城的母亲。
-> DONE

=== zh_0609 ===
// source: "The border matches the dry riverbed. It records hunger and thirst as her cause of death."
边纹和干涸的河床一致。它记下了她的死因：饥渴而死。
-> DONE

=== zh_0610 ===
// source: "The same child. Look at the way he is held. The man carrying him is his father in Night City."
同一个孩子。看他被背着的样子。背他的人是他在夜城的父亲。
-> DONE

=== zh_0611 ===
// source: "The path was uneven, but it was not a dangerous climb. He kept searching beyond the permitted waking hours and failed to reach a sleeping coffin in time."
路不平，但不算险。他一直找，超出了允许清醒的时限，没能及时回到睡棺。
-> DONE

=== zh_0612 ===
// source: "Bring the Scholar's disappearance report. We need the time her husband vanished."
把学者的失踪记录找来。我们需要知道她丈夫消失的时间。
-> DONE

=== zh_0613 ===
// source: "The diary writer carved memorials and came to question the stories they were asked to preserve. She was a funerary artist. Perhaps this was the one stone she could finally let speak for herself."
写日记的人刻过墓碑，也开始怀疑自己被要求留下的那些故事。她是一位墓碑设计师。也许只有这座碑，终于可以替她自己开口。
-> DONE


=== zh_0615 ===
// source: "A translated copy of designer manuscript\nOur cemetery usually represents a person through an icon of their occupation. This burial is different: the deceased is an infant who had not yet been assigned an occupation. None of the existing designs would do.\n\nThe family asked us not to define the child by work he had never begun. We chose a human figure instead. The child had no occupation, but he was still a person.\n\n\"A child without an occupation is a person before anything else.\""
设计师手稿译文
我们墓园通常用职业图案纪念死者。这次不同。逝者是一名尚未获分配职业的婴儿，旧有的设计一个也不适用。

家属请我们不要用孩子从未开始的工作定义他。于是我们选了一个人形。他没有职业，也依然是一个人。

「没有职业的孩子，首先也是一个人。」
-> DONE

=== zh_0616 ===
// source: "Clinical examination: The infant was covered in thick hair. His eyes barely opened. The attending physicians judged that he would be unable to adapt to conditions in Day City.\n\nAuthorization: Both parents signed the consent form.\n\nOutcome: Euthanasia was approved and carried out. Death was confirmed by the attending physician."
临床检查：婴儿全身覆盖浓密毛发，眼睛几乎睁不开。主诊医师判断其无法适应昼城的环境。

授权：父母双方已签署同意书。

结果：安乐死获批准并已执行。主诊医师确认死亡。
-> DONE

=== zh_0617 ===
// source: "The family's chosen depiction does not match with the records of the infant's appearance. The tombstone's expression of natural death does not settle what actually happened to him. There may be unexplained circumstances behind this death."
家属选用的形象与婴儿的相貌记录不符。碑上写的是自然死亡，孩子实际遭遇了什么仍未确定。他的死可能另有隐情。
-> DONE

=== zh_0618 ===
// source: "The unexplained disappearances in Day City are always reported at dawn, when people wake.\n\nThe Dayfolk's bodies are unusual. Anyone who fails to enter a sleeping coffin on time will die. Once inside, however, they lose all awareness and ability to act for the entire night, under the coffin's complete protection.\n\nWho has been tampering with their sleeping coffins? I cannot investigate the movements of the Nightfolks while they are awake. I can only suspect that, while taking our food, they have also done something to my husband and my people.\n\nIt is not only disappearances. Many of us, myself included, have found fresh wounds upon waking. Given the Nightfolk's habit of plundering, they are most likely responsible. I must remain vigilant."
昼城不明原因的失踪总是在人们醒来的黎明报告。

昼民的身体很特殊。不按时进入睡棺，就会死。可一旦躺进去，整夜都会失去知觉和行动能力，由睡棺全权保护。

是谁动了他们的睡棺？夜民醒着时在做什么，我无从查起。我只能怀疑，他们拿走食物的同时，也对我的丈夫和族人做了什么。

消失并不是唯一的问题。不少人醒来时发现身上多了新伤口，我也一样。夜民素来掠夺，最可能就是他们干的。我得提高警惕。
-> DONE

=== zh_0619 ===
// source: "The record describes a Day City resident who first studied this transparent mineral and discovered the energy within it. She was granted the title of Scholar.\n\nThe stones were later used to power machinery. The occupational title thus became associated with crystal research.\n\nA young man from a wealthy family was the first to invest in her research. He later became her husband and came to be known as the Tycoon.\n\nIn recognition of her outstanding contributions to Day City, the Scholar may apply for a mausoleum beyond the usual grave-marker design and have her family interred within it. For the Dayfolk, who place such importance on the rituals of death, this is the highest honor."
记录说，一名昼城居民最先研究这种透明矿物，发现里面蕴含的能量，于是得到学者的称号。

后来晶石被用来驱动机械，这个职业称号也因此与晶石研究相连。

第一个投资她研究的是一名富家青年。他后来成了她的丈夫，人称大亨。

为表彰她对昼城的卓越贡献，学者可以申请一座规格超出普通墓碑的墓室，将家人一同安葬。昼民看重身后礼仪，这对他们而言是最高荣誉。
-> DONE

=== zh_0620 ===
// source: "A legend of the Crystal God:\n\n\"When an infant with skin as smooth as crystal comes to Night City, the Nightfolk will see the light once more.\"\n\nThe child foretold in the prophecy was called the Divine Messenger."
一则关于晶石神的传说：

「当一名肌肤如晶石般光滑的婴儿来到夜城，夜民便会重见光明。」

预言中的孩子被称为神使。
-> DONE

=== zh_0621 ===
// source: "The human-shaped marker in Day City corresponds to the infant memorial in Night City. One city describes a death; the other commemorates a disappearance."
昼城人形小碑和夜城婴儿祭坛相互对应。一座城记的是死亡，另一座城纪念一次消失。
-> DONE

=== zh_0622 ===
// source: "The dry river border records a death from hunger and thirst. It connects the mother's fate with the loss of the underground water source."
干河边纹记着一场饥渴而死。它把这位母亲的遭遇与地下水源的消失联系了起来。
-> DONE

=== zh_0623 ===
// source: "The father left to search for the missing infant. The path itself was not a dangerous climb. He continued searching beyond the permitted waking hours and failed to return to a sleeping coffin in time.\n\nHis death can be compared with the report of the Scholar's husband disappearing at dawn."
父亲出门寻找失踪的婴儿。那条路本身并不危险。他一直找，超出了允许清醒的时限，没能及时回到睡棺。

可以把他的死亡与学者的丈夫在黎明消失的记录放在一起看。
-> DONE

